On 22 July 2020, Canadian [[Rock music|rock]] band [[Three Days Grace]] covered the song and released it as a non-album single.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://listen.tidal.com/album/149025767/credits|title=Three Days Grace – Somebody That I Used to Know|date=22 July 2020 |via=Tidal|access-date=28 July 2020|archive-date=28 July 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200728081533/https://listen.tidal.com/album/149025767/credits|url-status=live}}</ref> The song was later included as a bonus track on the Japanese version of the group's seventh album ''[[Explosions (Three Days Grace album)|Explosions]]''.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.sonymusic.co.jp/artist/threedaysgrace/discography/SICP-6457|title=エクスプロージョンズ|publisher=[[Sony Music Entertainment Japan]]|accessdate=4 February 2023|language=ja-JP|archive-date=4 February 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230204131300/https://www.sonymusic.co.jp/artist/threedaysgrace/discography/SICP-6457|url-status=live}}</ref> A [[music video]] (directed by Mike Filsinger) was also released for this version, which features the band performing in a [[Sketch (drawing)|Sketch]]-like background.<ref name="Loudwire">{{cite web|url=https://loudwire.com/three-days-grace-cover-gotye-somebody-that-i-used-to-know/|title=Three Days Grace Rock Up Cover of Gotye's Somebody That I Used to Know|website=[[Loudwire]]|author=Chad Childers|date=22 July 2020|access-date=4 February 2023|archive-date=4 February 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230204163316/https://loudwire.com/three-days-grace-cover-gotye-somebody-that-i-used-to-know/|url-status=live}}</ref> Their cover [[Three Days Grace discography#Singles|charted]] in the rock song charts of Canada and the United States. The song reached number seven on the ''[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]'' [[Canada Rock]] chart and number 19 on the US [[Rock Airplay]] chart.<ref name=CAR/><ref name=RKT/>

Lead vocalist [[Matt Walst]] noted about the song, saying: "The first time I heard 'Somebody That I Used to Know' I got goosebumps! This has only happened to me a few times in my life. I remember listening to it over and over and just being happy. Music releases a mood[-]enhancing chemical in the brain that can set good moods and peak enjoyment. Music is truly the best drug!"<ref name="Loudwire"/>

The track was produced by drummer [[Neil Sanderson]] and [[Howard Benson]].<ref name="Liner Notes">{{cite AV media notes|title=Somebody That I Used to Know|type=Digital liner notes|others=Three Days Grace|publisher=RCA Records|year=2020}}</ref> Bassist [[Brad Walst]] told ''Brave Words'' that Matt Walst sent him a voicemail of him singing the song with an acoustic guitar and Brad thought it would be a good idea to release a cover of it. The group recorded the track separately.<ref name="Brave Words">{{cite web|url=https://bravewords.com/features/three-days-graces-brad-walst-distinguished-gentlemen-among-young|title=Three Days Grace's Brad Walst – 'Distinguished Gentlemen Among Young'|website=Brave Words|author=Greg Prato|date=10 May 2022|access-date=15 April 2024}}</ref>

A music video was released on 22 July 2020, and was directed by Mike Filsinger.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://blabbermouth.net/news/three-days-grace-debuts-cover-of-gotyes-somebody-that-i-used-to-know|title=Three Days Grace Debuts Cover of Gotye's 'Somebody That I Used To Know'|website=[[Blabbermouth.net]]|date=22 July 2020|access-date=15 April 2024}}</ref> It was recorded on an [[iPhone]] with the band members performing in front of a white tarp and a filter was added on top of it after it was finished.<ref name="Brave Words"/>

