Electronic music producers, [[Fisher (musician)|Fisher]], [[Chris Lake]], and Sante Sansone reworked the song and released it as "Somebody (2024)" in February 2024.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.originmusicpublishing.com/news-items/remix-gotye-kimbra-fisher-chris-lake-sante-sansone-somebody-2024|title=REMIX: Gotye, Kimbra, FISHER, Chris Lake & Sante Sansone "Somebody (2024)"|website=Origin Music Publishing|date=15 February 2024|access-date=29 September 2025}}</ref> The single track is 2:33 minutes long.

====Reception====
At the [[2025 ARIA Music Awards]], the song was nominated for [[ARIA Award for Song of the Year]].<ref name="ARIA 2025 Noms">{{cite web | url = https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-09-25/aria-award-nominations-2025-aria-nominees-full-list/105815074 | title = ARIA Award nominations 2025: Ninajirachi, Dom Dolla, Amyl & The Sniffers lead the pack | publisher = Australian Broadcasting Corporation (ABC) | access-date = 26 September 2025 }}</ref>

Hugh McIntyre from ''[[Forbes]]'' said "It sounds almost exactly the same until about a minute in, when a big beat kicks in, and it becomes clear that something new has been added."<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/hughmcintyre/2024/02/26/gotyes-somebody-that-i-used-to-know-is-a-hit-all-over-again/?sh=519d0c9516dd|title=Gotye's 'Somebody That I Used To Know' Is a Hit All Over Again|website=[[Forbes]]|author=Hugh McIntyre|date=26 February 2024|access-date=15 April 2024}}</ref>

