Dutch DJ [[Tiësto]] remixed the song for his album ''[[Club Life: Volume Two Miami]]''.<ref>{{cite web |author=Akshay Bhansali |date=24 April 2012 |title=Tiesto's ''Club Life – Volume Two Miami'' a Tribute to City He Loves |url=http://www.mtv.com/news/articles/1683811/tiesto-club-life-miami-tribute.jhtml |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120430021850/http://www.mtv.com/news/articles/1683811/tiesto-club-life-miami-tribute.jhtml |archive-date=30 April 2012 |access-date=13 May 2012 |publisher=MTV}}</ref>

The [[a cappella]] group [[Pentatonix]] covered the song on YouTube video in February 2012, later releasing the track on their EP ''[[PTX, Volume 1]]'', on 26 June 2012.<ref>{{cite web |date=19 June 2012 |title=PTX volume 1 |url=https://itunes.apple.com/us/preorder/ptx-volume-1/id534570842 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120616002302/http://itunes.apple.com/us/preorder/ptx-volume-1/id534570842 |archive-date=16 June 2012 |access-date=19 June 2012 |publisher=iTunes (Apple)}}</ref> [["Weird Al" Yankovic]] recorded a cover as part of his polka medley "[[List of "Weird Al" Yankovic polka medleys#"NOW That's What I Call Polka!"|NOW That's What I Call Polka!]]" for his 2014 album ''[[Mandatory Fun]]''.<ref name="LinerNotes">''Mandatory Fun'' ([[liner notes]]). [["Weird Al" Yankovic]]. [[RCA Records]], a division of [[Sony Music]] Entertainment. 2014.</ref>

The song has been covered twice on [[BBC Radio 1]]'s [[Live Lounge]]: by [[Rita Ora]] in February 2012,<ref>{{cite web |date=15 February 2012 |title=BBC Radio 1Xtra Programmes – Trevor Nelson, DJ Fresh in the 1 Xtra Live Lounge, Rita Ora – 'Somebody I Used to Know' (Live Lounge) |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/p00p6rlr |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121210224208/http://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/p00p6rlr |archive-date=10 December 2012 |access-date=13 May 2012 |publisher=BBC (British Broadcasting Corporation)}}</ref> then by [[Fun (band)|fun.]] and [[Hayley Williams]] in May 2012.<ref>{{cite news |title=Fun Gotye Hayley Williams Video 'Somebody That I Used to Know' BBC Radio 1 Live Lounge 2012 |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GCim_0MZ2qI |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120516234025/http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GCim_0MZ2qI&gl=US&hl=en |archive-date=16 May 2012 |access-date=16 May 2012}}</ref>  In May 2012, American duo [[Karmin]] made a cover of the song on [[Sirius XM Radio|Sirius XM Hits]]as did [[Ray William Johnson]] through his project, Your Favorite Martian, published on Youtube May 23.<ref>{{cite web |last=Wieselman |first=Jarett |date=9 May 2012 |title=Karmin Covers Gotye's Omnipresent Hit |url=http://www.theinsider.com/music/52149_Karmin_Somebody_That_I_Used_To_Know_Gotye_Cover/index.html |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120712140401/http://www.theinsider.com/music/52149_Karmin_Somebody_That_I_Used_To_Know_Gotye_Cover/index.html |archive-date=12 July 2012 |access-date=22 October 2012 |work=The Insider |publisher=CBS Studios, Inc}}</ref> "Somebody That I Used to Know" has been covered by many other artists, including [[Ingrid Michaelson]], [[The Fergies]], [[Benee]], [[Sam Tsui]],<ref>{{cite news |last=Bell |first=Crystal |date=3 April 2012 |title=''Glee'' Covers Gotye: 11 Best 'Somebody That I Used to Know' Covers |url=https://www.huffingtonpost.com/2012/04/03/glee-gotye-somebody-that-i-used-to-know_n_1400324.html#s838688&title=Ingrid_Michaelson |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120510195521/http://www.huffingtonpost.com/2012/04/03/glee-gotye-somebody-that-i-used-to-know_n_1400324.html#s838688&title=Ingrid_Michaelson |archive-date=10 May 2012 |access-date=13 May 2012 |work=[[HuffPost]] |publisher=[[AOL]] ([[Arianna Huffington]], [[Kenneth Lerer]], [[Jonah Peretti]])}}</ref> Right the Stars featuring [[Karmina]],<ref>{{cite news |last=Bose |first=Lilledeshan |date=1 February 2012 |title=Gotye's 'Somebody That I Used to Know': The Five Best Covers |url=http://blogs.ocweekly.com/heardmentality/2012/02/gotyes_somebody_that_i_used_to.php |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120522021327/http://blogs.ocweekly.com/heardmentality/2012/02/gotyes_somebody_that_i_used_to.php |archive-date=22 May 2012 |access-date=13 May 2012 |work=[[OC Weekly]]}}</ref> [[Coheed and Cambria]],<ref>{{cite news |title=Coheed and Cambria, 'Somebody That I Used to Know': Band Covers Gotye Hit |url=http://www.noisecreep.com/2012/04/30/coheed-and-cambria-somebody-that-i-used-to-know-gotye/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120526220722/http://www.noisecreep.com/2012/04/30/coheed-and-cambria-somebody-that-i-used-to-know-gotye/ |archive-date=26 May 2012 |access-date=26 May 2012}}</ref> and [[Ray William Johnson|Your Favorite Martian]].<ref>{{cite news |title='Somebody That I Used to Know' (Gotye cover) |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2ogDd6xEBas |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120524012913/http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2ogDd6xEBas&gl=US&hl=en |archive-date=24 May 2012 |access-date=23 May 2012}}</ref>

[[Phillip Phillips]] and [[Elise Testone]] covered the song while competing on the [[American Idol season 11|eleventh season]] of ''[[American Idol (season 11)|American Idol]]'' on 11 April 2012.<ref name="tvbythenumbers128848">{{cite web |last=Bibel |first=Sara |url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2012/04/12/wednesday-final-ratings-modern-family-csi-american-idol-survivor-law-rock-center-down/128848/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120415010908/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2012/04/12/wednesday-final-ratings-modern-family-csi-american-idol-survivor-law-rock-center-down/128848/ |url-status=dead |archive-date=15 April 2012 |title=Wednesday Final Ratings: ''Modern Family'', ''CSI'', ''American Idol'', ''Survivor'', ''Law & Order: SVU'' Up; ''Rock Center'' Down |publisher=TVbytheNumbers |date=12 April 2012 |access-date=12 April 2012 }}</ref> and ''[[The Voice of Ireland (series 2)|The Voice of Ireland]]'' by Andy Mac Unfraidh.<ref>{{cite news |last=Judkis |first=Maura |date=17 April 2012 |title=Gotye's 'Somebody That I Used to Know': The breakup song's ubiquity |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/blogs/arts-post/post/gotyes-somebody-that-i-used-to-know-the-breakup-songs-ubiquity/2012/04/17/gIQAg1tQOT_blog.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141223182921/http://www.washingtonpost.com/blogs/arts-post/post/gotyes-somebody-that-i-used-to-know-the-breakup-songs-ubiquity/2012/04/17/gIQAg1tQOT_blog.html |archive-date=23 December 2014 |access-date=31 May 2012 |newspaper=The Style Blog, [[The Washington Post]]}}</ref>

English fingerstyle guitarist [[Mike Dawes]] released an arrangement of the song on his debut album ''What Just Happened?'' in 2013, garnering praise from Gotye.<ref>{{cite web |title=LMG Interview with Gotye &#124; Featured Interviews |url=http://www.livemusicguide.com/blog/featured-interviews/lmg-interview-with-gotye.html |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131003222009/http://www.livemusicguide.com/blog/featured-interviews/lmg-interview-with-gotye.html |archive-date=3 October 2013 |access-date=29 January 2013}}</ref> Jazz pianist [[Jacky Terrasson]] included the song in his 2015 album ''[[Take This]]''.<ref>{{cite web |last1=collar |first1=Matt |title=Take This – Jacky Terrasson {{!}} Songs, Reviews, Credits {{!}} AllMusic |url=https://www.allmusic.com/album/take-this-mw0002794152 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210314191655/https://www.allmusic.com/album/take-this-mw0002794152 |archive-date=14 March 2021 |access-date=25 September 2020 |publisher=[[AllMusic]]}}</ref>

Gotye paid tribute to the large number of cover versions of the song by creating a video remix, released in August 2012, using segments from hundreds of online covers to create a new, unique version of the track, titled "Somebodies: A YouTube Orchestra".<ref name="SomebodiesOrch">{{cite web |last=De Backer |first=Wally (Gotye) |date=13 August 2012 |title=Somebodies: A YouTube Orchestra |url=http://gotye.com/reader/items/somebodies-a-youtube-orchestra-209.html |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131005192642/http://gotye.com/reader/items/somebodies-a-youtube-orchestra-209.html |archive-date=5 October 2013 |access-date=9 September 2013 |publisher=Wally (Gotye) and GEA-Interactive Pty Ltd}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=12 August 2012 |title=Somebodies: A YouTube Orchestra |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=opg4VGvyi3M |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121221001750/http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=opg4VGvyi3M |archive-date=21 December 2012 |access-date=20 December 2012 |publisher=Gotye}}</ref> Gotye states the concept "was directly inspired here by Kutiman's [[Thru-You]] project", released in March 2009, which edited numerous YouTube videos to create a new cohesive song.<ref name="SomebodiesOrch" />

On 4 March 2025, [[Doechii]] officially released her single "[[Anxiety (Doechii song)|Anxiety]]" to digital streaming platforms after it went viral on [[TikTok]].<ref name="Mamo2025">{{Cite magazine |last=Mamo |first=Heran |date=March 4, 2025 |title=Doechii Drops 'Anxiety' Single: Stream It Now |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/doechii-anxiety-single-listen-1235915226/ |access-date=March 7, 2025 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> The song, which prominently samples "Somebody That I Used to Know",<ref name="Mamo2025" /><ref name="Chelosky2025">{{Cite web |last=Chelosky |first=Danielle |date=March 5, 2025 |title=Doechii Shares New Song "Anxiety": Listen |url=https://www.stereogum.com/2299200/doechii-anxiety/music/ |access-date=March 7, 2025 |website=[[Stereogum]]}}</ref> was originally recorded for her 2019 self-released mixtape, ''Coven Music Session, Vol. 1.''<ref>{{Cite web |last=Watts |first=Marina |date=March 5, 2025 |title=Doechii Finally Releases 'Anxiety' — a Song That She Recorded in Her Bedroom in 2019 |url=https://people.com/doechii-releases-anxiety-song-11691188 |access-date=March 7, 2025 |website=[[People (magazine)|People]]}}</ref> "Anxiety" was sampled by [[Sleepy Hallow]] for his [[Anxiety (Sleepy Hallow song)|2023 song of the same name]],<ref name="Chelosky2025" /> before Doechii's original demo became popular on [[TikTok]].<ref name="Mamo2025" />

